Actually, let me reconsider the whole thing. The stack-buffer-overflow WRITE. Let me look at the `imap_state_listsearch_resp` again:

```c
char *line = conn->data->state.buffer;
size_t len = strlen(line);
...
line[len] = '\n';
result = Curl_client_write(conn, CLIENTWRITE_BODY, line, len + 1);
line[len] = '\0';
```

The buffer is `buffer_size + 1` bytes. `strlen(line)` returns the length up to the null terminator. The null terminator is at position `n` where `n <= buffer_size`. So `len <= buffer_size`. Then `line[len] = '\n'` writes at `buffer[len]` where `len <= buffer_size`. Since buffer is `buffer_size + 1` bytes, `buffer[buffer_size]` is valid. So no overflow here.

